glacierphonk/naming
https://github.com/glacierphonk/naming
Copyright (c) 2026 GlacierPhonk

  - references/searchability.md: the Wikipedia-collision check, the
    "name + category" search, and the ladder from "no qualifier needed" to
    "unsearchable", mapped to a 1-5 score (from availability.md, "SEO and
    Searchability").
  - references/sound-symbolism.md: the consonant families (stops, fricatives,
    nasals, liquids), the front/back vowel size effect, ending sounds, and a
    feeling-to-sound matching table (from phonosemantics.md).
  - references/taglines.md: the length limit, the swap-in-a-competitor
    genericness test, the "don't restate the name" and buzzword-stacking
    warnings, and the glance/billboard test (from taglines.md).
  - references/scoring.md: the 1-5 anchored scale and ordered tie-breakers
    (from evaluation.md). The six criteria are this skill's own.
  - references/competitor-scan.md: searching for how competitors are named
    before generating (from SKILL.md, "competitor conflict search first").

cofoundy/brand-skills
https://github.com/cofoundy/brand-skills
Copyright (c) 2026 Cofoundy SAC

  Its skills/naming is itself adapted from glacierphonk/naming (per its own
  NOTICE); anything traced to that base is credited to GlacierPhonk above.
  Taken from Cofoundy's own additions:
  - SKILL.md, step 1: when two intake answers conflict, name the tension and
    get a priority before generating.
  - references/searchability.md: a free registry name does not mean the name
    is clear; check what already exists under it.

